    {
      "id": "e183",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1270,
      "y": 150,
      "width": 514.8000000000001,
      "height": 630.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 974471218,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 24795554,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Each fan has five connections.\n\nFan 1\n  • pin 11 → 100 Ω → fan blue   (speed control)\n  • pin 13 → 1 kΩ → fan green   (speed signal)\n  • 10 kΩ from pin 13's side of the 1 kΩ → 3V3\n  • fan black → GND rail,  fan yellow → 12 V rail\n\nFan 2 — the same, on other pins\n  • pin 12 → 100 Ω → fan blue\n  • pin 14 → 1 kΩ → fan green\n  • 10 kΩ from pin 14's side of the 1 kΩ → 3V3\n  • fan black → GND rail,  fan yellow → 12 V rail\n\nPull-down — 1 kΩ from each fan's BLUE wire to ground.\n  Fan side of the 100 Ω (between it and the fan).\n  Stops the fans when the controller has no power.\n\nAlso: board GND → GND rail. The supply's − and the\nboard must share ground, or nothing works.\n\nPins (left block, chip up, USB down):\n  outer column, 4th / 5th / 6th holes: 12, 13, 11\n  inner column, bottom hole: 14\n\n12 V goes ONLY to the fans' yellow wires —\nnever onto any hole of the board.\nSwitch the 12 V supply on last, keep USB plugged in.",
      "originalText": "Each fan has five connections.\n\nFan 1\n  • pin 11 → 100 Ω → fan blue   (speed control)\n  • pin 13 → 1 kΩ → fan green   (speed signal)\n  • 10 kΩ from pin 13's side of the 1 kΩ → 3V3\n  • fan black → GND rail,  fan yellow → 12 V rail\n\nFan 2 — the same, on other pins\n  • pin 12 → 100 Ω → fan blue\n  • pin 14 → 1 kΩ → fan green\n  • 10 kΩ from pin 14's side of the 1 kΩ → 3V3\n  • fan black → GND rail,  fan yellow → 12 V rail\n\nPull-down — 1 kΩ from each fan's BLUE wire to ground.\n  Fan side of the 100 Ω (between it and the fan).\n  Stops the fans when the controller has no power.\n\nAlso: board GND → GND rail. The supply's − and the\nboard must share ground, or nothing works.\n\nPins (left block, chip up, USB down):\n  outer column, 4th / 5th / 6th holes: 12, 13, 11\n  inner column, bottom hole: 14\n\n12 V goes ONLY to the fans' yellow wires —\nnever onto any hole of the board.\nSwitch the 12 V supply on last, keep USB plugged in.",
      "fontSize": 18,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    }
  ],
